Um, but he'll, he'll shoot at you or it, it's just like a ball.

00:12:33.260 --> 00:12:34.360
It shoots at you.

00:12:34.360 --> 00:12:39.560
And I, I would just hide under the, under the bottom one, fly up real fast to the top

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:43.320
one. And then like, I'd have to just kind of watch where the ball's following me and get it to

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:46.720
run into the top. And I wouldn't do that over and over again, get one or two shots in every time.

00:12:46.900 --> 00:12:49.900
And it took me forever, but, but I was able to beat it.

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:53.260
But yeah, I also noticed a major, uh, difficulty spike at that point.

00:12:53.380 --> 00:12:57.080
Yeah. I think that from like, it wasn't like I died on the mini boss.

00:12:57.220 --> 00:13:01.160
I think that's just where I noticed like, oh wow, this game is a lot harder than it made

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:03.100
itself seem like just two minutes ago.

00:13:03.100 --> 00:13:08.660
Yeah. And it's, it's deceiving because, because the controls are so one to one.

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:11.320
And I think that this game does have really good controls.

00:13:11.540 --> 00:13:18.060
It's that same. I mean, we've touched upon it before where, um, it seems like a deserved, uh, failure

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:18.920
when you die.

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:20.940
Um, sometimes it's just overwhelming.

00:13:21.160 --> 00:13:25.280
Well, I was going to say, okay, so I do think I agree with you on the deserved part.

00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:30.680
Like, you know, you realize that you deserved it except for this one idea that like, if you

00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:34.360
come in contact with an enemy, you should auto die.

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:39.380
I'm not a fan of that idea. Like, what is the point of having energy and health bars if, if just, if just, yeah.

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:45.360
If at the end of like touching something, like why is, this is just a problem I have in NES

00:13:45.360 --> 00:13:47.780
games and games that do one hit kills in general.

00:13:47.780 --> 00:13:50.260
It's like, why are they always able to kill me?

00:13:50.440 --> 00:13:53.960
Why isn't there like an opportunity for me to just like punch that guy in the face and

00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:54.960
take him down instead?

00:13:55.580 --> 00:14:01.440
Or just like they, maybe they have the same impact, uh, weakness that you do so that like

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:03.120
maybe they can die once in a while.

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:07.500
I think it would just be nice, a nice little variety, but I guarantee you no NES game programmed

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:08.400
it that way. No.

00:14:08.500 --> 00:14:11.500
Where sometimes you're the one hit kill and sometimes you get one hit kill.

00:14:11.500 --> 00:14:13.220
Oh, that would actually be really frustrating.

00:14:13.220 --> 00:14:15.660
Was it, uh, did Mach Rider do something like that?

00:14:15.740 --> 00:14:18.000
Where sometimes you would knock someone down, sometimes they would knock you down?

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:20.720
Well, I mean, if you, if you collided with anything that was just it.

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:22.620
Was it? You would blow up.

00:14:22.780 --> 00:14:24.000
Yeah. At least if it was head on.

00:14:24.100 --> 00:14:26.980
If you, if you just grazed it, you could, you bounced off.

00:14:26.980 --> 00:14:29.180
That's right. Yeah. From the side, from the side.

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:31.220
Yeah. You can do from the side, you would bounce off.

00:14:31.360 --> 00:14:34.640
And I think you could even, you know, if you were good enough at the game, you could

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:38.220
anticipate like a shove in Mach Rider to shove them over to the barrels.

00:14:38.260 --> 00:14:39.120
Oh yeah, I did some of that. That was fun.

00:14:39.160 --> 00:14:40.000
That would, that would be really cool.

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:42.160
This is not the Mach Rider nostalgia hour.

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:43.440
Absolutely not.

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:46.020
We just want to see how many times we can talk about something else.

00:14:46.020 --> 00:14:46.960
I w

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:53.100
Thank you.

00:15:20.500 --> 00:15:27.660
So, yeah, a different mechanic in the game that I rarely use just because it was kind of complicated and didn't work every time.

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:38.040
When you push A and B together to get that missile to spawn in the middle of the stage, like, it just glows and then you have missiles for, like, a little bit.

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:43.900
Yeah, I used it a couple times, but I was always too focused on just trying to shoot things.

00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:44.860
Yeah, exactly.

00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:49.460
I didn't see myself having an opportunity to be like, you know what, now I could really use the missile for what's coming up ahead.

00:15:49.620 --> 00:15:52.560
Like, I'd rather just focus on where things are coming at me.

00:15:52.620 --> 00:15:54.320
I kind of forgot the missile was even there.

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:58.280
I just kind of was too busy trying to not die.

00:15:58.440 --> 00:16:03.660
Especially because you do get power-ups in the game, and I think that those power-ups are pretty useful.

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:05.980
Yeah, it does make your gun look pretty sweet.

00:16:06.560 --> 00:16:13.280
I think there's, like, four or five, but there's, like, one that is just a combination of two of them.

00:16:13.360 --> 00:16:18.000
And it's like, that's the one I really want, but I think you need both prior to get that one.

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:21.680
And I think they have, like, mega names or something like that.

00:16:21.760 --> 00:16:26.220
Mega names? No, like, each one's, like, the mega buster or the mega doomer.

00:16:26.640 --> 00:16:27.460
Oh, okay, the doomer.

00:16:28.580 --> 00:16:29.700
I'm making that up.

00:16:29.840 --> 00:16:33.260
Those are not the titles, but I couldn't be bothered to look them back up.

00:16:33.440 --> 00:16:40.100
Yeah. Because, to be honest, this is, you know, we're talking about, like, the gameplay and stuff like that.

00:16:40.300 --> 00:16:47.880
But I didn't want to get too into the difficulty right away because it just, it does get so hard after a while that I didn't feel encouraged.

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:57.120
Especially because when you die, like, all everything, you get flown back to the beginning of the section.

00:16:57.300 --> 00:16:58.980
Yeah. And you have to start all over.

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:10.020
That is part of, like, okay, I don't truly understand what gives you, like, a regular game over screen and what makes you fly back to the beginning of it.

00:17:10.120 --> 00:17:12.100
Like, sometimes I would just die and restart.

00:17:12.600 --> 00:17:16.700
And then sometimes I would die and start outside the base again.

00:17:16.700 --> 00:17:18.540
Mm-hmm. And do you know what that was?

00:17:18.680 --> 00:17:21.000
Like, I ran out of lives both times.

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:23.360
I think I always died and just started from the beginning.

00:17:23.760 --> 00:17:24.960
You never saw the fly back?

00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:26.960
But there's, like, the fly, doesn't it fly you back to the beginning?

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:27.860
It flies you back, yeah.

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:31.580
But then you have a certain amount of lives and then there's a game over.

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:34.100
Yeah. Gotcha. But it still flies you right back to the very beginning.

00:17:34.100 --> 00:17:35.660
So you get, like, one continue or something.

00:17:35.660 --> 00:17:36.780
Yeah, you get, like, one continue.

00:17:36.840 --> 00:17:38.180
Okay. I gotcha.

00:17:38.260 --> 00:17:40.320
Yeah. But, I mean, like, a cool mechanic.

00:17:40.980 --> 00:17:42.200
Yeah. In practice.

00:17:42.640 --> 00:17:45.560
But the checkpoints are too far out for a game this hard.

00:17:46.360 --> 00:17:54.380
You have to get to section 19 and defeat the boss to get to section, I guess, like, 20 would be next.

00:17:54.960 --> 00:18:01.140
To get to section 20 and then that's, like, if you die from that point on, you'll just get blown back to section 20.

00:18:01.460 --> 00:18:02.700
Because how many are there?

00:18:02.740 --> 00:18:05.500
Are there 60? There are way too many levels in this game.

00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:07.380
Yeah, there's a lot. There are 60 in the NES.

00:18:07.380 --> 00:18:10.320
So there's three checkpoints, I'm assuming, if it's on every 20.

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:12.120
19. Which I did not get to a checkpoint.

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:13.460
I will get that.

00:18:13.740 --> 00:18:17.940
I actually just assumed, like, okay, it's numbered now.

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:20.000
It's not 26 levels.

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:20.840
They added levels.

00:18:21.060 --> 00:18:22.560
So this makes sense.

00:18:22.760 --> 00:18:25.000
I thought maybe there would be 30 levels.

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:27.320
To be honest, I was expecting the 26 still.

00:18:27.720 --> 00:18:28.700
Just to end at 26?

00:18:28.700 --> 00:18:29.580
Just to end at 26.

00:18:29.700 --> 00:18:31.820
Be like, oh, well, that's how many letters in the alphabet.

00:18:32.180 --> 00:18:33.780
And that would be section Z.

00:18:33.820 --> 00:18:35.940
I didn't know that they changed it.

00:18:36.080 --> 00:18:37.680
Like, I didn't look at the arcade first.

00:18:37.820 --> 00:18:39.140
Yeah, neither did I. So I didn't know that they had changed it yet.

00:18:39.140 --> 00:18:40.940
I just assumed, okay, 26 sections.

00:18:41.560 --> 00:18:47.600
So what happened then was, like, okay, I exhausted my ability to play the game.

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:51.440
I was, in some parts I was frustrated, in some parts I was bored.

00:18:52.040 --> 00:18:54.220
But I did enjoy a lot of the time that I was playing it.

00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:56.680
So I'm like, okay, I want to see what else this game has to offer.

00:18:56.680 --> 00:18:58.740
I will watch a speed run of this game.

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:02.420
And the speed run for this game is 40 minutes long.

00:19:02.540 --> 00:19:06.120
That's crazy. And it is, like, 60, yeah, it's 60 levels.

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:09.120
And they all are pretty long, like, levels.

00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:13.440
Right. And it's kind of crazy because in an NES game, usually the speed runs aren't that long.

00:19:13.520 --> 00:19:20.560
No. But also, it's, you know, there's really no way to do it faster because you are at the mercy of the speed.

00:19:21.100 --> 00:19:26.540
And at the very, not to get on a tangent, but at the very beginning, at the very start, you're going real fast.

00:19:26.880 --> 00:19:28.260
And then they're like, nah, no, just kidding.

00:19:28.260 --> 00:19:29.120
And we're going to sell you down.

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:35.580
That's because you're outside, though. There are moments in the game where, like, later while you're in the base that you go that fast.

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:36.660
But they're pre...

00:19:36.660 --> 00:19:42.660
Yeah, those are, like, section five, for instance, is one where it's like, you know, hey, you picked the right room.

00:19:42.860 --> 00:19:45.720
Like, you can just skip right through this and go to the next stage.

00:19:45.880 --> 00:19:52.820
Whereas, like, the other option, I think, would send you to section eight that would give you, like, a cool power-up if you found it.

00:19:52.940 --> 00:19:54.640
But otherwise, you have to fight, like, a bunch of enemies.

00:19:54.640 --> 00:19:58.400
Mm-hmm. Unless you have something that you would like to talk about.

00:19:58.400 --> 00:20:04.360
I just wanted to move on to where I think the length is really...

00:20:04.360 --> 00:20:05.840
It really hurts the game.

00:20:06.060 --> 00:20:07.080
Okay. Let's hear it.

00:20:07.080 --> 00:20:15.740
Because I don't think that it's impossible for a game to feel worthy of that kind of length, especially in the NES time.

00:20:15.920 --> 00:20:17.940
Mm-hmm. But the...

00:20:17.940 --> 00:20:26.660
Just, like, the lack of variety in, like, the kinds of bosses you fight, the enemies, I just...

00:20:26.660 --> 00:20:29.220
It doesn't seem to warrant being that long.

00:20:29.340 --> 00:20:32.200
Aside from just, like, here's a new pattern, I guess?

00:20:32.360 --> 00:20:37.380
Like, it just seems like different permutations of the same enemies, and then you get the same boss.

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:42.720
It definitely feels like they made it longer, knowing that the arcade version is only the 26 levels.

00:20:42.860 --> 00:20:50.480
It does feel like they made it longer just because it's a console game and they wanted, you know, you to hold onto it longer and have more to play.

00:20:50.600 --> 00:20:55.740
Yeah. Kind of like they did that just by spreading it out, not adding new stuff, taking what was there and, like, duplicating it.

00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:57.600
Yeah, exactly. Like, making more of the same.

00:20:57.740 --> 00:21:02.020
I think it would have been cool as, like, a sense of accomplishment, though, to split that into, like, a game A and game B.

00:21:02.020 --> 00:21:07.240
You know, kind of like, hey, cool, you beat the easy mode, now play the hard mode.

00:21:07.240 --> 00:21:08.340
Now play endurance mode.

00:21:08.940 --> 00:21:10.200
Right, something different.

00:21:10.840 --> 00:21:17.480
Let me ask you guys, would you have preferred a linear path, or was the choice thing, like, a cool mechanic that you didn't mind?

00:21:17.760 --> 00:21:24.440
If I'm being totally honest, I don't think I've played this long enough to appreciate the fact that there are choices.

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:29.640
But, like, as you guys are saying, too, it is cool to be able to take a different path.

00:21:29.640 --> 00:21:40.120
I mean, I think just for a game like this in general, I guess I would go multiple paths as long as it didn't, like, hinder the level design.

00:21:40.220 --> 00:21:43.120
If the level design gets sloppy because they're making too many paths, then of course.

00:21:43.220 --> 00:21:49.580
Right, and I do think sometimes the level design gets sloppy because you go down, like, some wrong ones later on, and you get punished pretty hard.

00:21:49.720 --> 00:21:51.060
You get sent back pretty far.

00:21:51.220 --> 00:21:56.940
And I don't think that that's, like, the appropriate way to hurt the player at that stage in the game.

00:21:56.940 --> 00:22:00.340
Like, they've made it, they've been playing for that long, and then you send them back a little further.

00:22:00.640 --> 00:22:01.920
I don't think that's the way to do it.

00:22:02.040 --> 00:22:10.340
But I just want to talk to you real fast, Joe, because you were saying that even though you only played for a little bit of time, did you not feel a sense of choice when you were going through the quarters?

00:22:10.540 --> 00:22:13.680
I didn't. I mean, I, you know, obviously there's two paths.

00:22:13.900 --> 00:22:17.820
But I didn't, when I went through, I guess I didn't expect the other path to be that different.

00:22:18.100 --> 00:22:22.280
Gotcha. Because it was, I was still new to the game, too, so I wasn't sure what to expect.

00:22:23.500 --> 00:22:26.680
Maybe I wasn't giving enough credit, but, like, are the paths that different?

00:22:26.980 --> 00:22:30.880
They are. I mean, because you can skip entire portions of the game.

00:22:30.920 --> 00:22:41.720
And I think that's why I do like that, because a player that really enjoys playing this game and has played it a lot will eventually find an optimal path.

00:22:41.840 --> 00:22:45.060
Right. Or at least the path that they find the most enjoyment out of.

00:22:45.060 --> 00:22:51.400
I am a fan of the choice thing, and I would actually like, I would have liked to have seen it in even, like, other genres.

00:22:51.940 --> 00:23:01.820
Well, it's kind of, I think what Joe was saying is he felt that it was more like in Mock Rider, how you can pick, like, one of the two spaghetti strands.

00:23:02.020 --> 00:23:03.940
Oh, okay. And they just sort of, like, feel the same.

00:23:03.980 --> 00:23:06.480
Right, right. But we know that they're different tracks.

00:23:06.740 --> 00:23:17.340
Yes. That is kind of what, without having the, without having gone back to choose different routes to, like, back up the fact that it would feel the same, that was just my gut feeling.

00:23:17.480 --> 00:23:19.260
It was like, what am I really picking here?

00:23:19.380 --> 00:23:21.040
Gotcha, gotcha. Okay.

00:23:21.680 --> 00:23:22.760
One other question.

00:23:23.060 --> 00:23:25.940
Is the protagonist too big for the stage?

00:23:27.220 --> 00:23:29.220
I felt like he was a little big.

00:23:29.460 --> 00:23:32.280
I mean, I can see why you'd say that.

00:23:32.280 --> 00:23:34.400
I think he was an appropriate size.

00:23:34.400 --> 00:23:35.660
I mean, maybe he bumps in as he wants.

00:23:35.660 --> 00:23:39.680
It would be hard to dodge after a while if too many enemies were on the screen because of the size.

00:23:39.680 --> 00:23:43.640
Oh, I definitely found it was hard, but I don't know if I would have done any better if he was smaller.

00:23:44.340 --> 00:23:46.360
I feel like I could have slipped through a little more.

00:23:46.440 --> 00:23:50.900
I guess now that you mentioned it to me, not even on a gameplay level, just on a, like, what are we fighting?

00:23:51.040 --> 00:23:53.320
Because you're kind of fighting spaceships, right?

00:23:53.420 --> 00:23:56.520
Yeah, you're fighting weird, like, mechanical objects.

00:23:56.760 --> 00:23:58.140
There's even turrets though, too.

00:23:58.220 --> 00:24:00.340
Yeah, you're right. The turrets are, like, the size of, like, your ankle.

00:24:00.340 --> 00:24:01.460
Of your leg? Yeah.

00:24:02.560 --> 00:24:09.320
So then I was thinking, like, I guess now if I'm looking back on it, like, who's, there's nobody in those spaceships because they're smaller.

00:24:09.680 --> 00:24:10.700
Well, yeah, they're robots.

00:24:11.460 --> 00:24:12.520
The tiny little robots.

00:24:12.740 --> 00:24:17.760
Yeah. Gotcha. What did we think of those, that intro and the cut scenes?

00:24:18.380 --> 00:24:25.060
Well, there are only, like, two cut scenes, three if you include the, like, you fucked up cut scene.

00:24:25.140 --> 00:24:28.720
Right. But, like, I don't know, they looked nice.

00:24:28.720 --> 00:24:29.960
I thought they looked really nice.

00:24:30.060 --> 00:24:31.720
Yeah. Like, I actually appreciated that pixel art.

00:24:31.780 --> 00:24:35.300
And there was some good world building at the very start, you know?

00:24:35.440 --> 00:24:38.180
Like, seeing your character kind of, like.

00:24:38.180 --> 00:24:42.660
Is that world building? I think it's at least, like, giving me a sense of purpose in this game.

00:24:43.100 --> 00:24:43.940
Yeah, purpose, context, sure.

00:24:44.040 --> 00:24:45.020
Yeah, I gotcha. Yeah.

00:24:45.380 --> 00:24:46.440
Sorry, not world building.

00:24:46.440 --> 00:24:49.720
I guess more, like, you know, at least there's some lore to this rather than just, like.

00:24:50.000 --> 00:24:53.660
Even the fact that you don't start inside the base is kind of cool.

00:24:53.860 --> 00:24:55.240
Yeah. If we're being honest, you know?

00:24:55.360 --> 00:24:59.200
Like, yes, everything gameplay-wise didn't work out so well here.

00:24:59.200 --> 00:25:05.280
But I think that they did do some cool things to make some nice touches and make it feel like a little more, you know.

00:25:05.400 --> 00:25:06.440
Like an adventure.

00:25:07.000 --> 00:25:09.220
Yeah, an adventure. I don't want to say cinematic because it didn't feel cinematic.

00:25:09.460 --> 00:25:11.220
But, yeah, adventure feels like the right word.

00:25:11.320 --> 00:25:12.540
You are going on a journey.

00:25:12.780 --> 00:25:14.260
Not the Rygar style.

00:25:14.280 --> 00:25:16.780
No, no, no. Not quite as grand.

00:25:17.440 --> 00:25:19.020
You do do some stuff.

00:25:19.060 --> 00:25:25.540
But I do think that it would have, now just marrying that idea with, again, the idea of the multiple paths.

00:25:25.540 --> 00:25:32.320
I think it would have been kind of cool to have the multiple paths if there were, like, secret unlockable power-ups on certain paths.

00:25:32.340 --> 00:25:33.580
Oh, but there are. They're, like, buried in there.

00:25:33.700 --> 00:25:34.840
Oh, there you go. Well, there you go.

00:25:35.020 --> 00:25:36.520
Boy, do I have a game for you.

00:25:36.700 --> 00:25:37.980
It's called Section Z.

00:25:38.900 --> 00:25:42.520
Yeah, I mean, you know, this is the stuff that the casual player is not going to find.

00:25:42.520 --> 00:25:45.420
But it will reward the other players that seek it out.

00:25:45.920 --> 00:25:53.460
There are, like, you know, if you go into a certain section, that's the only place that you're going to find, you know, like, this power-up for a while.

00:25:53.460 --> 00:26:01.520
Or it's, like, do you remember there were, like, those, like, circular tubes that were, like, they were, like, purple?

00:26:01.800 --> 00:26:09.720
Yeah. If you stand over some of those, they will form, like, an entrance for you and you'll get sucked into, like, a mini stage.

00:26:09.900 --> 00:26:15.720
Oh, I know. And then in there, there will either be, like, some enemies to clear out or a new weapon.

00:26:17.240 --> 00:26:18.480
Yeah, some new power-ups.

00:26:18.660 --> 00:26:20.280
Like, so it's there.

00:26:21.120 --> 00:26:25.260
But what's really strange about that is that you do have to stand on those platforms.

00:26:25.360 --> 00:26:28.620
It's not just going to, like, show itself, be like, hey, you found the right thing.

00:26:28.620 --> 00:26:29.560
Because you're hovering over it.

00:26:29.620 --> 00:26:31.640
Yeah, yeah, yeah. It's going to be like, hey, you found the right thing.

00:26:31.740 --> 00:26:33.120
It's like, nope, you have to look for it.

00:26:33.220 --> 00:26:36.540
I do think it's a good, just talking about standing.

00:26:37.120 --> 00:26:42.440
I think it's a cool touch that if you are low enough to the ground, you will just, like, plant your feet.

00:26:42.680 --> 00:26:44.240
Yeah. And actually walk.

00:26:44.340 --> 00:26:46.080
There's a walk animation. You walk and stuff.

00:26:46.200 --> 00:26:49.300
And I know that that's not, like, oh, it's so advanced.

00:26:49.500 --> 00:26:50.840
Like, no, it's just cool. I don't know.

00:26:51.540 --> 00:26:53.380
They definitely didn't have to program.

00:26:53.380 --> 00:26:54.720
No, you could have just hovered.

00:26:54.800 --> 00:27:03.300
Yeah, exactly. And there was also those, like, those, like, cyst-looking creatures that if you shot them, they would give you power-ups, too.

00:27:03.400 --> 00:27:05.740
So there were a couple different ways to get power-ups.

00:27:05.740 --> 00:27:08.080
And I think that, you know, that's not my problem.

00:27:08.360 --> 00:27:15.380
Thankfully, this is not a Metroidvania-style game where you have to, like, explore the sections, find the power-ups to get further on.

00:27:15.560 --> 00:27:19.140
Because imagining a Metroidvania shmup is just—

00:27:19.140 --> 00:27:20.320
Nope. No, no thank you.

00:27:20.640 --> 00:27:25.740
The shmup genre is hard enough as is and, you know, has its share of fans.

00:27:25.780 --> 00:27:27.220
I don't think we need that.

00:27:27.380 --> 00:27:33.980
But if there was going to be a mechanic or an item added to this game, what would you guys add?

00:27:33.980 --> 00:27:39.140
I think the easy answer for me is just more save points.

00:27:39.320 --> 00:27:41.900
Or not save points, but, you know, more checkpoints.

00:27:42.040 --> 00:27:52.300
No, seriously. Would you have preferred a save point thing, maybe, where it's, like, a certain section is just, like, you know, like a place to save and maybe, like, recover some health?

00:27:52.940 --> 00:27:56.140
Yeah. Or even if there's a challenge aspect to it.

00:27:56.240 --> 00:27:59.580
It's, like, you know, there's this one enemy that's hard to beat.

00:27:59.580 --> 00:28:03.520
You can just pass it. But, like, if you beat this enemy, it's a checkpoint or something.

00:28:03.680 --> 00:28:05.860
That's kind of cool. Just some way to make it—

00:28:05.860 --> 00:28:08.380
In a way, that is the bosses, though, if you think about it.

00:28:08.400 --> 00:28:09.840
Yeah, I guess that's true. But you have to beat the boss.

00:28:09.940 --> 00:28:12.000
Right. Stage 19, it's like you—

00:28:12.000 --> 00:28:12.820
Yeah, I see what you're saying.

00:28:12.820 --> 00:28:19.860
You're kind of asking for optional save points throughout that require some sense of skill but then reward the player for doing that.

00:28:19.860 --> 00:28:21.040
It's like a risk versus reward thing.

00:28:21.220 --> 00:28:27.120
I'm only saying that to—what's the phrase I'm looking for?

00:28:27.260 --> 00:28:35.140
To find a happy medium or split the difference between what they've given us and what I want, which is more save points.

00:28:35.140 --> 00:28:39.620
Yeah, I think you've actually struck that because that is, like, that is something I could see them actually implementing,

00:28:39.620 --> 00:28:44.280
knowing, like, how the rest of the game goes in the sense of, like, hey, you might find these things along the way,

00:28:44.320 --> 00:28:50.140
but also your game—the game is completely playable with you just never picking up a power-up, never doing—

00:28:50.140 --> 00:28:53.780
I mean, like, it's incredibly hard and stupid, but it is playable.

00:28:53.780 --> 00:29:00.560
You could theoretically just defeat the final boss by shooting your little laser at it like a thousand times.

00:29:01.660 --> 00:29:08.240
I think that my feature—again, it's, I guess, something to make it a little easier,

00:29:08.240 --> 00:29:13.320
but also to add another layer of, like, of depth and, like, a skill ceiling.

00:29:14.280 --> 00:29:19.780
Because you were saying that there—if you touch an enemy or certain projectiles,

00:29:19.800 --> 00:29:23.500
because I guess they count as solid, you'll just die.

00:29:23.520 --> 00:29:28.740
I think, like—and it's tricky with the NES controller because there are only so many inputs,

00:29:28.740 --> 00:29:37.780
but if maybe you were able to press the shoot button and the directional button in, like, the direction of the enemy or the object,

00:29:37.980 --> 00:29:42.240
like, you could do, like, a parry thing where it would be, like, a melee attack.

00:29:42.360 --> 00:29:46.400
Yeah, yeah, yeah. But it would have to be, like, something that required precision so that you could just spam it.

00:29:46.580 --> 00:29:55.220
Reminds me of kind of what they did in Metroid Samus Returns for 3DS where they added melee to her arsenal

00:29:55.220 --> 00:29:58.420
so this way she can actually fight back the creatures that try to attack her.

00:29:58.720 --> 00:30:04.140
Obviously different because she's not floating through space, but, like, you know, same idea.

00:30:04.400 --> 00:30:05.240
I'll say this.

00:30:05.240 --> 00:30:12.120
I think it would be really cool if instead of, like, having the power-ups be something you find

00:30:12.120 --> 00:30:15.760
and then, like, you know, you activate them, and once you activate them, if you want a different one,

00:30:15.840 --> 00:30:17.840
then you'll lose that other power-up.

00:30:17.940 --> 00:30:22.340
I think it would have been kind of cool to, like, spread the power-ups out a little more

00:30:22.340 --> 00:30:27.680
and then instead have the power-ups be, like, choosable through the select option.

00:30:27.920 --> 00:30:32.060
So, like, you know, it's like once you've found, you know, and this weapon's not even in the game,

00:30:32.140 --> 00:30:33.540
but just imagine if they added more of those.

00:30:33.700 --> 00:30:38.460
It's like once you've found the ice beam, now you can freeze enemies in their tracks, you know,

00:30:38.520 --> 00:30:42.120
and it's like it doesn't kill them and they will eventually defrost,

00:30:42.120 --> 00:30:45.120
so you'll want to, you know, also shoot them with the other weapons,

00:30:45.120 --> 00:30:47.260
so it's kind of like toggling all your different weapons.

00:30:47.340 --> 00:30:48.880
I feel like that would have been a cool thing to do.

00:30:48.880 --> 00:30:53.460
Yeah, I think that would add another layer of depth to the game as well.

00:30:53.660 --> 00:30:54.680
Also, open world.

00:30:54.900 --> 00:30:55.740
Open world, yeah.

00:30:56.440 --> 00:30:57.480
3D open world.

00:30:57.560 --> 00:30:59.560
3D open world MMORPG.

00:31:00.120 --> 00:31:04.000
Yeah. Also, it should have a Battle Royale as well.

00:31:05.940 --> 00:31:07.940
It should be Battle Royale schmuck.

00:31:08.880 --> 00:31:09.820
Whoa, can we do that?

00:31:10.020 --> 00:31:11.300
I feel like, yeah.

00:31:11.300 --> 00:31:12.320
You need a lot of people.

00:31:12.860 --> 00:31:14.880
A lot of people. There's just got to be tons of players in there.

00:31:36.160 --> 00:31:40.680
So, I just want to talk about the arcade differences and get your guys' reaction on this

00:31:40.680 --> 00:31:46.780
because we talked about how this was a pretty hard game and I'd like to see if you would have preferred the arcade version

00:31:46.780 --> 00:31:48.700
or said, no, they made the right changes here.

00:31:50.020 --> 00:31:52.520
So, I'll say right off the bat, it's practically a different game.

00:31:52.540 --> 00:32:00.200
I did play the arcade one and it controls differently in the sense that A and B don't work like that.

00:32:00.200 --> 00:32:04.940
Instead, A changes your direction and B is your shoot button.

00:32:05.240 --> 00:32:10.920
So, you have to click a tire button just to change to which sides and then you shoot with a totally different button.

00:32:11.120 --> 00:32:17.600
I feel like what they did with the NES game was getting around, Sean, what you were talking about with Commando and stuff,

00:32:17.680 --> 00:32:23.520
just getting around the thing that most games at this time had a problem with was that your turning in one direction

00:32:23.520 --> 00:32:25.040
has also made you move in that direction.

00:32:25.660 --> 00:32:33.500
I feel like this arcade controller took a step towards getting around that problem but then put it back.

00:32:34.780 --> 00:32:36.860
Here's another button that gives you the same problem.

00:32:37.020 --> 00:32:41.700
Then the arcade version came first, so it's kind of funny to think that Capcom had this eureka moment

00:32:41.700 --> 00:32:44.580
where they were like, oh, you don't need separate buttons.

00:32:45.400 --> 00:32:47.580
You can just both do the same thing.

00:32:47.860 --> 00:32:51.200
So, that's one thing that's different in the arcade version.

00:32:51.200 --> 00:32:56.680
The other is that there are five stages and five sections and then the final boss stage.

00:32:56.780 --> 00:32:59.120
So, there's only 26 stages instead of 60.

00:32:59.800 --> 00:33:00.660
Yeah. We cool with that?

00:33:00.800 --> 00:33:09.780
I prefer a – I think that if they put more variety in those 26 levels and they kept the difficulty,

00:33:10.220 --> 00:33:15.020
you could still – it would still feel like a complete game because, again, we couldn't get to 20.

00:33:15.200 --> 00:33:17.140
Yeah, I definitely couldn't get to 26.

00:33:17.140 --> 00:33:20.720
26. Automatic death when hit by fire.

00:33:20.920 --> 00:33:24.580
And what I want to say to that is there is no energy whatsoever.

00:33:24.900 --> 00:33:26.540
Everything is a one-hit kill.

00:33:26.960 --> 00:33:27.940
Wow. Everything.

00:33:28.140 --> 00:33:29.540
There's none of that energy meter stuff.

00:33:29.600 --> 00:33:35.040
I mean, that makes sense because of the quarter-eating element of arcades.

00:33:35.240 --> 00:33:37.840
But I definitely wouldn't want that on my NES.

00:33:37.920 --> 00:33:40.640
I feel like if you were playing this in the arcade and you picked it up on the NES,

00:33:40.900 --> 00:33:43.080
you're just going to be a monster at this game.

00:33:43.160 --> 00:33:44.840
It's like you've been swinging with three bats.

00:33:46.720 --> 00:33:53.660
And then last, the Famicom Disk System version, the kids in Japan are laughing at us because,

00:33:53.880 --> 00:33:59.460
of course, just like every other Famicom Disk game, this bad boy can save at any section,

00:33:59.460 --> 00:34:02.060
at any moment. At any moment.

00:34:02.060 --> 00:34:03.160
Sorry. No, I don't. At any moment.

00:34:03.160 --> 00:34:03.980
Like saving of it.

00:34:05.080 --> 00:34:06.280
No, that's cheating.

00:34:07.480 --> 00:34:09.640
No, but yes, it can save at different sections.

00:34:09.640 --> 00:34:12.640
And so there's no risk of like, oh, I got to wait until section 19.

00:34:12.640 --> 00:34:13.540
Like, right.

00:34:13.800 --> 00:34:19.060
The one thing that I will say that I prefer the NES version over the arcade version is

00:34:19.060 --> 00:34:23.480
because I did watch a little bit of the arcade version, so I couldn't get a handle on like how it felt.

00:34:23.640 --> 00:34:30.400
Okay. But I do think it has a more cohesive look to it on the NES.

00:34:30.400 --> 00:34:31.480
I was going to say that, yeah.

00:34:31.740 --> 00:34:35.960
On the arcade, it just sort of looks like a bunch of, I mean, I'm not going to say.

00:34:37.740 --> 00:34:41.500
It's not Atari style, like 20, like those old, old arcade games.

00:34:41.500 --> 00:34:47.860
No, it's not like that, but I'm not going to say that they just used a bunch of like free assets to create everything,

00:34:48.000 --> 00:34:54.220
but it doesn't have like, it doesn't thematically look like the backgrounds and the foregrounds look like they're in the same game.

00:34:54.620 --> 00:34:59.800
Yeah, I think this is maybe our first instance of getting, and maybe it's just because it's so different,

00:34:59.980 --> 00:35:04.600
of getting a better game on the NES than in the arcade.

00:35:04.900 --> 00:35:06.100
Yeah, I think so too.

00:35:06.100 --> 00:35:10.500
I think that, you know, even just because there's so many differences, that's why it's better,

00:35:10.520 --> 00:35:15.920
because we've seen a lot of times, even games we really like, we go and play the arcade versions of them,

00:35:15.960 --> 00:35:18.100
and we're like, oh, well, the arcade version was better.

00:35:18.240 --> 00:35:21.140
But like in this instance, I'm not totally on board for that.

00:35:21.200 --> 00:35:25.100
I know that like there's better effects, and it's got a higher pixel count than the arcade,

00:35:25.240 --> 00:35:27.740
but it just doesn't, it doesn't feel the same.

00:35:28.620 --> 00:35:33.100
And so Section Z did kind of get like two more games,

00:35:33.100 --> 00:35:37.880
but I don't think they're on NES, and they're just kind of like, they're loosely tied together.

00:35:38.140 --> 00:35:43.580
I think it's more of just like, these two games also came from Capcom and involved those kind of same elements,

00:35:43.620 --> 00:35:46.480
and that's Sidearms and Forgotten Worlds.

00:35:46.560 --> 00:35:48.340
We'll probably never play them.

00:35:48.940 --> 00:35:52.900
Okay. Just, you know, like if we ever get that far chronological.

00:35:53.220 --> 00:35:54.800
We have to die someday, Sean.

00:35:55.160 --> 00:36:00.780
No. All right, I think it's time for Joe to have a thought.

00:36:01.020 --> 00:36:06.900
Straight thought. And I'm really not, I've never been seriously thinking about making this a thing,

00:36:07.060 --> 00:36:12.420
but I have to talk about the pause sound, because the pause sound in this game actually is wild.

00:36:13.460 --> 00:36:14.800
Please, please describe.

00:36:14.800 --> 00:36:18.460
I can't even describe it because I can't fully, there's too many notes in it, I can't remember it.

00:36:18.520 --> 00:36:19.520
Can you play it here?

00:36:19.760 --> 00:36:20.720
I'll play it here.

00:36:21.940 --> 00:36:23.160
That wasn't that wild.

00:36:24.140 --> 00:36:25.400
I just don't, I just.

00:36:25.400 --> 00:36:29.540
I don't remember it, so I'm going to have to now like listen to the episode and tweet my comments.

00:36:29.800 --> 00:36:34.420
I just had it, thought it was funny because I'm always like joking about the pause sound,

00:36:34.500 --> 00:36:36.780
and then I was kind of like, I kind of got to mention this pause sound.

00:36:36.840 --> 00:36:38.300
This one's like actually over the top.

00:36:38.420 --> 00:36:40.220
I think. Joe's pause sound corner.

00:36:40.420 --> 00:36:44.540
I want that to be like an article, like an updated article that you just kind of like

00:36:44.540 --> 00:36:46.440
every now and again when you notice pause sounds.

00:36:46.540 --> 00:36:49.180
I don't want to hear like every single pause sound.

00:36:49.280 --> 00:36:52.320
I just want the ones that you've like, hey, you know, I noticed this one.

00:36:52.580 --> 00:36:54.700
Yeah. Right. And that's my straight thought.

00:36:55.020 --> 00:36:56.700
Yeah. So you found yourself pausing a lot.

00:36:57.460 --> 00:37:00.200
It was actually just when I was, when I was done, when I was about to shut it off.

00:37:00.300 --> 00:37:01.720
I like paused it and I was like, oh shit.

00:37:02.380 --> 00:37:03.880
Go pause sound. Whoa, you can pause it?

00:37:03.880 --> 00:37:04.820
I like this game now.

00:37:04.940 --> 00:37:07.680
You also, that means you also found out you can pause right then and there.

00:37:07.880 --> 00:37:08.840
That's right. I hadn't paused it before.

00:37:08.860 --> 00:37:10.440
It's like, I don't think that you can pause.

00:37:10.760 --> 00:37:14.040
I mean, every game I've tried to pause and I've been able to pause so far.

00:37:14.240 --> 00:37:15.380
Volleyball had restrictions.

00:37:15.640 --> 00:37:16.440
Oh yes, they did.

00:37:16.780 --> 00:37:17.700
Oh yeah. Timeouts.

00:37:17.700 --> 00:37:20.440
I knew somebody could save me for saying something dumb.

00:37:21.240 --> 00:37:22.180
I got your back.

00:37:22.340 --> 00:37:23.860
Yeah. Thank you. Okay.

00:37:23.880 --> 00:37:27.500
So I think now we can go into the essential games list.

00:37:30.140 --> 00:37:34.080
So last time we recorded an episode, I said I wasn't going to say, all right guys, it's

00:37:34.080 --> 00:37:37.780
time for the essential games list and I have something different prepared, but I don't.

00:37:37.980 --> 00:37:40.640
There's really like no way to like go right into it.

00:37:40.780 --> 00:37:44.520
So instead, Sean, I'd like you to get right into it with your vote.

00:37:45.160 --> 00:37:51.840
All right. Well, I think that this is a, I enjoyed playing this game for the most part.

00:37:51.840 --> 00:37:59.700
Um, again, uh, one thing our listeners might notice is that I don't take difficulty very

00:37:59.700 --> 00:38:01.740
well, um, on first impressions.

00:38:02.080 --> 00:38:04.260
Uh, I get frustrated pretty easily.

00:38:04.700 --> 00:38:07.800
Um, but I don't think I don't, that's not a knock on the game.

00:38:08.300 --> 00:38:11.020
I think that the game is way too long for its own good.

00:38:11.280 --> 00:38:13.300
I did praise its aesthetic.

00:38:13.460 --> 00:38:18.920
Um, but I also think that a lot of the environments are kind of samey.

00:38:18.920 --> 00:38:25.380
Um, there's only so much you can do with like the three or four, I don't know, like tile

00:38:25.380 --> 00:38:26.540
sets that they were using.

00:38:27.120 --> 00:38:35.620
Um, I think that the monster design or like just the enemy design, uh, had a lot to, um,

00:38:36.520 --> 00:38:38.620
like there's a, there was a lot like on the table there.

00:38:38.780 --> 00:38:43.840
I think they could have done with it, but it was just like turrets and a couple like spider

00:38:43.840 --> 00:38:45.440
thingies. And that was about it for me.

00:38:45.440 --> 00:38:50.980
Um, I think that they could have done a lot more to spice this game up, but it's core.

00:38:51.140 --> 00:38:52.220
It is an enjoyable game.

00:38:52.400 --> 00:38:55.900
It's not a pass. Definitely play this game, but I don't find this game essential.

00:38:56.940 --> 00:39:03.580
Joe. I think the good things about this game, which, which maybe we didn't talk about this enough

00:39:03.580 --> 00:39:07.640
is that I think the controls, especially with the A and B are really cool and it feels really

00:39:07.640 --> 00:39:11.360
good and it feels responsive and it feels fast and you feel like a badass.

00:39:11.360 --> 00:39:19.040
Um, and that actually like made me really enjoy this game at the beginning, but it is a little

00:39:19.040 --> 00:39:25.520
too repetitive for how long it is and just long in general that after a while it gets,

00:39:26.280 --> 00:39:29.340
it gets boring or I mean, I don't want to say boring.

00:39:29.740 --> 00:39:30.620
It gets stale. Exactly.

00:39:30.820 --> 00:39:34.260
It was never like, it was never yawning while I was playing it, but it was just like, I

00:39:34.260 --> 00:39:37.120
don't know if I, I don't know if I care enough to finish this game.

00:39:37.120 --> 00:39:41.380
One thing I would like to just jump in, uh, piggyback off you is, uh, I think the music

00:39:41.380 --> 00:39:46.360
in this game is really good, but because, and like the music also isn't just like an eight

00:39:46.360 --> 00:39:50.100
bar loop. It actually has some musical progression to it too.

00:39:50.380 --> 00:39:55.180
Um, but there are only like four songs and you're going to be hearing those four songs

00:39:55.180 --> 00:39:55.980
a lot.

00:39:56.220 --> 00:40:01.220
So in the same vein of like, for 60 levels, they could have had more than four songs.

00:40:01.640 --> 00:40:03.680
There's good stuff, but it's too repetitive.

00:40:04.040 --> 00:40:07.800
Right. Uh, yeah, I think that was kind of, that kind of sums up my, my thoughts overall.

00:40:08.120 --> 00:40:09.820
So what's your vote? There were some cool things.

00:40:10.100 --> 00:40:11.820
Wasn't quite enough to keep me entertained.

00:40:12.120 --> 00:40:14.000
Not essential, but I'd say play it.

00:40:14.200 --> 00:40:18.900
Okay. There were entire minutes where I had fun playing this game.

00:40:19.320 --> 00:40:24.120
Uh, and I don't mean that as like a dig because there are certain NES games where I never had

00:40:24.120 --> 00:40:29.980
fun to begin with. Uh, I can list like five already and we're only on game like 50 something.

00:40:31.220 --> 00:40:35.160
So for me, it's not that, um, it's not that this game is bad.

00:40:35.820 --> 00:40:36.940
And, uh, I agree.

00:40:37.000 --> 00:40:37.820
This game isn't boring.

00:40:38.000 --> 00:40:41.440
I think like for the right person, this could be a very, very fun game.

00:40:41.580 --> 00:40:48.620
And if you're the kind of guy who enjoys like a challenging, uh, shmup or early shmup too,

00:40:48.780 --> 00:40:50.980
like it's not, it's not the kind of shmups we think about today.

00:40:51.660 --> 00:40:54.200
For me, they're just, there's not enough to this game.

00:40:54.200 --> 00:40:58.180
It has the 1942 problem where like, oh, this is a really cool concept.

00:40:58.180 --> 00:41:00.960
And then I've seen everything I need to see very fast.

00:41:01.220 --> 00:41:07.000
And there's no sense of like, you know, progression as a character, even like, like I said, I would

00:41:07.000 --> 00:41:11.280
have loved to have some more power ups or even like some, you know, it doesn't, not every

00:41:11.280 --> 00:41:16.240
game has to have these RPG elements, but it certainly helps, especially when looking at

00:41:16.240 --> 00:41:20.660
through it, like today's lens, it certainly helps to make it feel like the game is growing

00:41:20.660 --> 00:41:21.460
as you play it.

00:41:21.460 --> 00:41:26.060
And with this one, I just kind of felt like, you know, if I start, if the game started mild,

00:41:26.220 --> 00:41:31.440
it pretty much went mild throughout, you know, like it didn't really pick up or, you know,

00:41:31.660 --> 00:41:37.020
or get any more exciting than the very first instant, you know, with that awesome cut scene.

00:41:37.740 --> 00:41:39.460
So for me, not essential.

00:41:39.760 --> 00:41:41.340
I don't know if I'd say play it.

00:41:41.460 --> 00:41:43.400
I think if you're a shmup fan, play it for sure.

00:41:43.600 --> 00:41:47.280
I think this one has like a neat control concept that every shmup person should try out

00:41:47.280 --> 00:41:49.240
just because it's a different way to tackle that genre.

00:41:49.240 --> 00:41:52.240
But I don't know if I'd say play this to most people.

00:41:52.400 --> 00:41:54.100
I think this one you can pass.

00:41:58.280 --> 00:41:59.300
All right. Cool.

00:41:59.560 --> 00:42:02.080
One last thing I want to talk about before we end this episode, though.

00:42:02.300 --> 00:42:03.600
T-shirts. What?

00:42:03.840 --> 00:42:04.820
Oh, I'm sorry. T-shirts?

