We got a great deal out of the back of a van, and I just figured let's sell.

00:42:16.580 --> 00:42:17.700
No, that's not what we're talking about.

00:42:17.980 --> 00:42:23.440
I'm talking to Sean for a minute because you mentioned that you, a lot of times, you don't

00:42:23.440 --> 00:42:26.320
like very difficult games, and you think it shows on the podcast.

00:42:26.560 --> 00:42:27.820
So I'm going to ask you this question.

00:42:28.340 --> 00:42:32.780
Do you need to be good at video games to host a video game podcast?

00:42:33.140 --> 00:42:34.020
I don't think so.

00:42:34.020 --> 00:42:39.860
Only because we've been doing it for a while, and I would consider at least you a host.

00:42:40.060 --> 00:42:51.280
Okay. And I think I've overstated that difficulty rubs me the wrong way, but when we have the volume

00:42:51.280 --> 00:42:53.540
of games, this is sort of like a behind-the-scenes thing.

00:42:53.660 --> 00:43:00.240
When we have the volume of games that we play for the show and are playing for our own enjoyment

00:43:00.240 --> 00:43:06.220
that may not have come out on the NES, it just gets frustrating when I can only get past

00:43:06.220 --> 00:43:11.360
a couple levels. I need that to color my commentary.

00:43:11.700 --> 00:43:13.380
Yes. You know what I mean?

00:43:13.640 --> 00:43:15.700
Yeah. Joe, different question.

00:43:15.940 --> 00:43:19.360
Sure. Do you have to be good at games to review them?

00:43:20.680 --> 00:43:22.000
I don't know if you have to be.

00:43:22.080 --> 00:43:24.780
I think you should be able to play games.

00:43:24.860 --> 00:43:29.260
You shouldn't give it to one of your parents that has to say, how do I go?

00:43:29.260 --> 00:43:36.240
You shouldn't be playing. But also, most people who are going to play the game aren't going to be amazing at the

00:43:36.240 --> 00:43:43.600
game. I mean, you want it from a perspective, I think, of someone that appreciates the game and learns

00:43:43.600 --> 00:43:45.360
it as they're playing, and maybe it gets good, maybe it doesn't.

00:43:45.380 --> 00:43:51.160
Imagine if only amazingly talented players played and reviewed Dark Souls.

00:43:51.340 --> 00:43:53.160
Like, if no one told you that it was hard.

00:43:54.180 --> 00:43:58.400
We need a review for that game where someone just says, yeah, you know what?

00:43:58.400 --> 00:44:00.360
And I couldn't finish it, and you probably won't either.

00:44:00.780 --> 00:44:03.360
Right. You know? I mean, that's how I feel about Bloodborne.

00:44:03.520 --> 00:44:06.200
I love that game, but I still have not finished that game.

00:44:06.620 --> 00:44:12.380
Even for me, anyone that's listening and anyone in this room would kick my ass in Super Smash

00:44:12.380 --> 00:44:14.460
Brothers. I'm just terrible at Super Smash Brothers.

00:44:14.460 --> 00:44:17.440
I don't play it that often. I don't have a Nintendo system.

00:44:18.900 --> 00:44:20.520
But I love Super Smash Brothers.

00:44:20.780 --> 00:44:21.980
I play it, and I'm like, this is fun.

00:44:22.160 --> 00:44:24.800
And I'm sure if I played it a lot, I'd be a lot better at it.

00:44:24.800 --> 00:44:29.320
But I don't play it a lot, but I can still pick it up and decide that it's a good game,

00:44:29.340 --> 00:44:31.280
even though most people are better than me at it.

00:44:31.420 --> 00:44:32.600
I think that's a great point.

00:44:32.980 --> 00:44:35.900
And what it comes down to is it's just like everybody plays games differently.

00:44:37.240 --> 00:44:41.860
And the cool thing about that is because everybody plays the games differently, you get a hundred

00:44:41.860 --> 00:44:42.780
different perspectives.

00:44:43.040 --> 00:44:46.580
